                            {
                                "target_word": "perch",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "23963bef-0057-3159-ae39-7c72fe606310",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfb7376-38cb-3707-b253-1e804ace5def",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rest on a perch (especially, of a bird); to roost."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa0cc526-97b6-4662-b7fe-e547cecbcfaf",
                                                "sense_id": "23963bef-0057-3159-ae39-7c72fe606310",
                                                "text": "The macaw perched on Jim's shoulder."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9efd738-4a73-325a-ab46-3aaa9d85f9ab",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfb7376-38cb-3707-b253-1e804ace5def",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sit upon the edge of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fe8deda-95a3-4c6e-9e14-f9335f3f8aa8",
                                                "sense_id": "e9efd738-4a73-325a-ab46-3aaa9d85f9ab",
                                                "text": "The platform was already crowded, but the newcomers threaded their way to the front amid a decorous murmur of welcome. Mr. Peeble shoved and exhorted and two end seats emerged upon which Enid and Malone perched themselves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0450081e-f8d8-359e-9fb0-3872198254fb",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfb7376-38cb-3707-b253-1e804ace5def",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stay in an elevated position."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38f19459-f8a8-3d0a-b2fc-2f0676793376",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfb7376-38cb-3707-b253-1e804ace5def",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To place something on (or as if on) a perch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46d34d60-bcb8-4095-bd59-16a382f17083",
                                                "sense_id": "38f19459-f8a8-3d0a-b2fc-2f0676793376",
                                                "text": "The most obvious beneficiary of the visitors' superiority was Frank Lampard. By the end of the night he was perched 13th in the list of England's most prolific goalscorers, having leapfrogged Sir Geoff Hurst to score his 24th and 25th international goals. No other player has managed more than the Chelsea midfielder's 11 in World Cup qualification ties, with this a display to roll back the years."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "523845c8-da60-32a1-bfb8-c20f5fef93e5",
                                        "entry_id": "fcfb7376-38cb-3707-b253-1e804ace5def",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To inspect cloth using a perch."
                                        ],
